    <statement><p>Certain radioactive material decays in such a way that the mass remaining 
after <m>t</m> years is given by the function
<me>m(t)=175 e^{-0.015 t}</me>
where <m>m(t)</m> is measured in grams.</p>
<p>(a) Find the mass at time <m>t=0</m>.</p>
<p>Your answer is <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(b) How much of the mass remains after 15 years?</p>
<p>Your answer is <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
